error: dynamic_newtype!: `MyStr` is not one of the shaped inner types. `String` and `Vec<u8>` are matched as literal tokens, so a type alias (e.g. `type MyStr = String`) or a fully-qualified path (e.g. `alloc::vec::Vec<u8>`) does NOT match them. If what you wrote IS a `String` or a `Vec<u8>` under another spelling, write the literal token to get the full API for that shape -- do NOT reach for `generic` to silence this, because the macro cannot see through a path or an alias either, and you would land on the reduced arm with the growable payload and none of the methods that handle it safely. `generic <type>` is for an inner type that is genuinely neither `String` nor `Vec<u8>`; it gives RevealSecret, RevealSecretMut, Debug, Zeroize, and `new`.
